This repository is licensed in three parts: the SKELETON (open), the BRAND
(reserved), and the FONTS (their own license). Some files, such as the token
files, contain both the skeleton and the brand values. In those files the
split below applies to their content.


1. SKELETON, CODE AND TOOLING - MIT License
===========================================

This part covers:

  - The code and tooling: scripts/, sd.config.mjs, .storybook/, stories/,
    .github/, package.json and package-lock.json.
  - The documentation: README.md, SKILL.md, CHANGELOG.md, FONTS.md,
    tokens/README.md, reference/checklist.md, and the "Integración" part of
    reference/guide.md (installation and recipes per stack).
  - The structure of the design system: the file layout of tokens/ and
    dist/, the W3C DTCG format, the core / semantic / theme layers, the names
    of the tokens and of the CSS custom properties, the alias relationships
    between tokens, the light/dark theme mechanism, and the way the system is
    built and published.

You can reuse the skeleton as the base of your own design system, as long as
you replace the brand values of part 2 with your own.

